The schema contains a stable vessel entity plus timestamp-specific observation, location, point, velocity, and orientation entities. It also contains structured geopolitical affiliations, structured MMSI and IMO alternate identifiers, and a last-port entity with its own UN/LOCODE identifier and country affiliation.

The vessel subject uses mmsi because MMSI is populated in every sample and identifies a vessel across stream updates. The other ship identifiers are modeled separately: ship_id is retained as the source-system identifier, while MMSI and IMO become AlternateIdentifier entities because the schema supplies multiple distinct identifier standards.

Each dynamic entity uses both mmsi and timestamp so observations from different stream updates do not merge. Location and AbsolutePoint are separate because bsm:hasGeographicLocation leads to Location and bsm:hasGeometry then leads to Geometry. Velocity and Orientation are also separate ontology entities. The speed column is not mapped to bsm:speedMetersPerSecond because values such as 84 are characteristic of encoded AIS speed rather than explicit metres per second, and arithmetic conversion is unavailable. Course maps to bsm:absoluteBearingAngle, while heading maps to bsm:headingAngle; the deciding qualifiers are course/track versus longitudinal-axis heading.

Flag is modeled as a GeopoliticalAffiliation because bsm:hasAffiliation explicitly covers vessel flag state. ship_country is not also mapped because it expresses the same affiliation as a country name while the available affiliation property specifically expects a code.

The populated last-port group evidences a separate maritime facility. The exact subtype is ambiguous: bsm:Port is qualified as civilian or commercial, while bsm:MilitarySeaportOrNavalBase requires a military qualifier that last_port does not supply. Therefore the safer class is bsm:MaritimeTransportFacility. Its UN/LOCODE is represented as an AlternateIdentifier because the group provides both a source port ID and a separately standardized code. Current-port and next-port entities are not emitted because all identifying fields are empty in every supplied record.

ais_type_summary maps to vesselCategoryCode because values such as Military are vessel categories. type_name maps to the free-text typeName property. shiptype is left unmapped because its numeric coding scheme is not declared. max_speed is also left unmapped: bsm:vesselMaximumSpeed is qualified as maximum design speed, whereas the stream column does not state whether it is design or observed maximum speed.

Every IRI transformation was checked against its referenced subject transformation: vessel_location_{mmsi}_{timestamp}, vessel_point_{mmsi}_{timestamp}, vessel_velocity_{mmsi}_{timestamp}, vessel_orientation_{mmsi}_{timestamp}, vessel_observation_{mmsi}_{timestamp}, affiliation_{flag}, alternate_mmsi_{mmsi}, alternate_imo_{imo}, affiliation_{last_port_country}, and alternate_unlocode_{last_port_unlocode} are character-for-character identical at each reference. No unnecessary transformation key is included.

